                <pb facs="0881" n="1839" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1839"/>

                <head>No. 14.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. White</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 9,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bayard stated, in reply to Mr. White’s telegram of April 7, that this
                    Government did not object to the extension of the arrangement for the protection
                    of the fur-seal fisheries to the whole of Behring Sea.</p>
            </div>
